WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.567
- Welcome to the show.
It is great to meet you.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.133
-Thanks for having me.
-And congrats on

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.801
all the success
of "White Lotus."

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:07.801
Golden Globe awards.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:10.334
Today, you just got nominated
for a SAG award.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:11.901
-Yeah.
-This is a big deal.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
Well-deserved.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:14.734
-Thanks.
-I'm going to read you a couple

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:16.734
reviews about you here.
-Oh, don't do that.

00:00:16.734 --> 00:00:18.267
-Plug your ears.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:20.467
"USA Today" says,
"Fahy is effervescent,

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.901
lighting up every scene
she's in."

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.133
-Oh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:26.834
-"Entertainment Weekly" said,
"Meghann Fahy

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:28.300
is flat-out incredible."

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.667
There you go. Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:34.567
You can't get better than that.
-That's so nice.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.067
-You know what is nice, though?

00:00:36.067 --> 00:00:38.000
I've been reading articles
about the cast,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.400
and you guys are all friendly
in talking about each other.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.133
And they said that you were

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:43.968
the nicest person
that they worked with

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:45.734
and they said that everyone out
of the cast,

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:48.901
you seem like
the most outgoing person.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:50.667
-Oh, wow.
-You would talk to everybody

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:53.601
and say hi to everyone.
-Oh, yes, well, that's true.

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:55.901
-Yeah?
-I think it's very important

00:00:55.901 --> 00:01:00.701
to, like, sort of know
your neighborhood.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.367
So, when I got to Sicily,

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:04.567
I wanted to make friends
with all the people.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.567
Because it's like, you know,
I'm a New Yorker

00:01:06.567 --> 00:01:09.067
and you've got to make friends
with the bodega guy.

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:10.467
-Absolutely.
-My bodega guy

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:12.467
installed my A.C.
-It's part of your neighborhood.

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:13.534
-Exactly.
-Yes.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:16.033
-So --
-You know bartenders.

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:17.434
-That's right.
You've got to get in.

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:18.667
Yeah.
-Yes.

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.501
So, in Sicily, you walked
around, introduced --

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:23.334
you said hi --
-Yeah, I felt like Belle

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:24.834
from "Beauty and the Beast"
sometimes.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.934
I'd be like walking down
the street

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:28.567
with my little basket
full of flowers.

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:31.300
And people would be like
sticking out the shop to say hi.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.067
It's very cute, yeah.
-"Hi, Meghann. Hi."

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:35.634
I heard you also did a cooking
class with one of the --

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:37.701
-Yeah, so I made friends with

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:39.367
the owner of one
of the restaurants.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:40.868
-This is what happened.
-And I mentioned that

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:42.234
I wanted to take
a cooking class.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:43.367
And he was like, "Well,
you should come here

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:44.701
and I'll give you one."

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:46.300
And I said, "Okay."

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.767
He said, "Just come
at noon tomorrow."

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.767
Which also, is like
kind of cool, right?

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.434
-Fantastic.
-No texting,

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:54.934
just show up to this place
at 12:00.

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:56.534
-Love Italy, yes.
-Yeah.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:59.067
So, I went, and then it wasn't
actually a cooking class,

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.634
because it just was me
in the kitchen

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.901
while the restaurant was open
and serving food.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:07.467
And I was just sort of
in the kitchen, like --

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:08.968
-Cooking?
-Cleaning things

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:11.934
and serving them to people.
-So, he gave you a job?

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:14.634
-Yeah, I had a chef hat on.
-Wow. You got a job.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.133
-He made me a gin and tonic.

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:17.901
We were --
-Fantastic.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:20.234
12:00, noon?
-[ Chuckles ] Yeah.

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:23.834
-But this show really
kind of kicks off with you.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:26.834
No spoilers,
but you discovering a dead body.

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:30.300
And is it a little bit relaxing

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.167
knowing that you're not the one
dying at the end of the show?

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:37.100
-Well, I have to tell you,
I read -- I read it.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.501
-Yeah.
-And I was like,

00:02:38.501 --> 00:02:40.200
"Okay, this character
finds the body."

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.834
But I didn't necessarily
feel like that meant

00:02:42.834 --> 00:02:45.634
that I still couldn't
potentially be dead.

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:49.200
You know? Like, because
you just don't know.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.701
-Oh, maybe it's
a dream sequence.

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:51.901
-Yeah, who knows?

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.133
-I mean, that's where
my brain goes.

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.400
-At first, I was like,
"Oh, cool, I'm alive."

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.667
And then I was like,
"Well, let's see.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:57.067
Let's read the rest
of this first to find out."

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:59.367
-So, you really didn't know?
-Yeah.

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:03.801
-I want to say because
I love Mike White obviously.

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:04.968
-Same.
-I know.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:05.968
Gosh, who doesn't love the guy?

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.067
But in the opening scene,

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:10.167
these two actors
are right there.

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:12.400
And these actually
weren't even really actors.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.767
These are --
-That's right.

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:16.067
-These are -- they were on
"Survivor" with Mike White.

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:18.100
-Yeah. Let's clap for them.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.767
They killed it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:22.934
So good.
-Kara Kay and Angelina Keeley.

00:03:22.934 --> 00:03:24.467
-Yes.

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:26.901
-Did you watch the "Survivor"
season with Mike White on it?

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:28.968
-I did. I had to.
-Me, too. I loved it.

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:30.968
-I had a couple of friends
who said,

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:32.868
"If you only watch
one episode of 'Survivor,'

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:34.734
it should be this one."
-I agree.

00:03:34.734 --> 00:03:36.167
-So, I watched it in Italy.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.968
And then when Mike told me --

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:40.834
because we shot that scene
sort of towards the end.

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:43.434
And when he told me that it was
going to be these two women

00:03:43.434 --> 00:03:45.868
that were doing the scene with
me, I was like fan girling.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:48.033
-And how are they as actors?
-Fantastic.

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.601
Angelina might be
the most committed.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:55.400
-Okay.
-She did cry a lot.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.968
There was one part we were
shooting the body being

00:03:57.968 --> 00:04:01.200
sort of pulled from the water.
-Yes.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.067
-And she really went for it.

00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:06.434
And Mike was like, "Angelina,
you've got to stop crying."

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:08.200
[ Laughter ]
-Really?

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.667
-Yeah.
He was like, "It's not sad.

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:12.501
It's spooky.
You don't know this person."

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:15.234
-[ Laughs ]
-And she was like, "Okay, damn."

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:16.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.067
But, no, they were amazing.

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:19.767
And I was actually so impressed

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:22.634
with how great they genuinely
were in that scene.

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:24.734
-It all worked perfect,
the casting,

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:27.367
all the way around were
just knockout performances.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.968
When, if you watch this season,
you'll be like,

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.801
"Oh, yeah, everyone's great."
But you were unbelievable.

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.767
Do you get asked about
the last scene?

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:35.701
I don't want to spoil anything
but --

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:38.200
-But let's spoil it.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.934
-I'm not going to spoil it.

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:42.434
But does anything happen?
Did anything happen?

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:44.200
-Yes. I think so.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.267
-What?

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:46.701
-Yes.
-What?!

00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:47.634
-You want me to tell you
what it was?

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:48.734
-What are you talking about?

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:50.400
Roots, play some music
for a little bit.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.968
-Just play some -- anything.

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:53.367
Just, yeah, what happened?

00:04:53.367 --> 00:05:00.667
♪♪

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.334
You think so?
-Yeah.

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:03.701
-Wow. Alright.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.767
Good. Wow.
-Thanks, guys.

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.501
-Wow. Yeah, that was it.

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:09.434
That was the spoiler.
I just heard it.

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:11.000
[ Applause ]

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.033
No, she didn't tell me anything.

00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:15.501
But do people come up and go,

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.868
"Hey, what did --"
Why would people ask?

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:20.400
You shot something
and didn't use it?

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.801
That was actually shot, right,
what you did?

00:05:22.801 --> 00:05:24.133
-Well, no, it wasn't,

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:26.000
which is what's so cool
about Mike.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.033
I feel like he's really
interested in sort of like...

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.934
-The mystery.
-...suggesting something

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:31.567
and then letting
the audience kind of decide

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.000
how they feel about it.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.567
Sort of open to interpretation.

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:38.334
So, even -- It was really funny

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:40.801
'cause I saw him
on the night of the finale.

00:05:40.801 --> 00:05:44.133
And I asked him, because
people ask me all the time.

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:45.167
-Yeah.
-I was like,

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:46.367
"What do you think happened?"

00:05:46.367 --> 00:05:48.501
And I told him
what I thought happened.

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:49.634
-Yeah.
-He was like, "Ew,

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:50.701
I don't want to think
about that."

00:05:50.701 --> 00:05:52.501
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.501 --> 00:05:54.734
I hate spoilers, and I don't
know how long you have to wait

00:05:54.734 --> 00:05:57.234
to talk about something,
because it's like,

00:05:57.234 --> 00:05:59.834
it's out and the ending is out,
but some people don't know

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:01.434
and I don't want to ruin
anything for anyone.

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:02.601
But it is fantastic.

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:05.434
Watch "The White Lotus,"
HBO Max, Meghann Fahy.

00:06:05.434 --> 00:06:06.501
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:08.100
Here's Meghann
in "The White Lotus."

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:11.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Cameron Hartford, why?

00:06:11.734 --> 00:06:14.000
-Maybe something happened.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.167
[ Waves crashing ]

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:21.901
[ Indistinct conversations
in distance ]

00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:39.634
-I don't think you have
anything to worry about.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.567
I mean, you never really
know what goes on

00:06:44.567 --> 00:06:47.701
in people's minds
or what they do, right?

00:06:47.701 --> 00:06:49.267
You spend every second
with somebody,

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:52.400
and there's still
this part that's a mystery.

00:06:53.868 --> 00:06:55.934
-Yeah! That's how you do it.

00:06:55.934 --> 00:06:58.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Meghann Fahy, everybody.

00:06:58.534 --> 00:07:01.501
All episodes of season 2
of "The White Lotus"

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.701
are available to stream
on HBO Max.

00:07:03.701 --> 00:07:05.300
More "Tonight Show"
when we come back.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:06.300
Stick around, everybody.

